---
title: Diffusion-limited aggregation
---
Fire particles at a small open seed. Each digs the last solid tile it crossed before it reached open floor [[t:103-108 s:13]].

## The rule
1. **Seed:** dig a plus of five tiles at the center of a solid map [[c05:19-40 t:103-104]].
2. **Until a third of the map is open** [[c05:43]]:
   1. start a particle on a random tile [[c05:49-52]];
   2. move it until it stands on open floor [[c05:53-80]];
   3. dig the last solid tile it stood on [[c05:53-82]].

The talk’s three versions differ in step 2 [[t:103-104 t:111-112 t:115-116]]:

{% table label="How a particle travels, by version" rowheads=true %}
* Version
* The particle moves
* It digs
---
* `walk` (c05)
* one random step at a time [[c05:55-80]]
* the last solid tile it stood on [[c05:55-82]]
---
* `attractor` (c06)
* along a straight line to the center [[c06:56-66]]
* the last solid tile it stood on [[c06:62-68]]
---
* `symmetric` (c07)
* along a straight line to the center [[c07:56-67]]
* that tile and its mirror image across the middle column [[c07:62-77]]
{% /table %}

