## Step through it
@@steps limit=5 mid=2

## Controls
@@control mode
How a particle travels. `walk`: a random step at a time. `attractor`: a line to the center. `symmetric`: the same, digging each tile’s mirror image too [[c05:55-80 c06:56-68 c07:56-77]].
@@control floor_divisor
Stop when 1 / this of the map is open. All three demos: a third [[c05:43 c06:43 c07:43]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

- **Talk says:** the simple version is very winding, and guaranteed to be contiguous [[t:109]].
- **Walk:** both hold. {{c05.regions.max}} region on every seed; {{c05.dead_ends.median}} dead ends at the median, vs cellular automata’s {{c03.dead_ends.median}} [[run:c05.regions.max c05.dead_ends.median c03.dead_ends.median]].
- **Attractor, symmetric:** not contiguous. {{c06.regions.median}} and {{c07.regions.median}} regions at the median; never fewer than {{c06.regions.min}} and {{c07.regions.min}} [[run:c06.regions.median c07.regions.median c06.regions.min c07.regions.min]].
  - **Why:** their particles follow a Bresenham line to the center [[c06:56-60 c07:56-60]]. A diagonal step on that line leaves the dug tile touching the cave only at a corner, and walking is four-way [[own]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

- **No cap in the talk’s code:** the simple version’s walk runs until it finds open floor [[c05:55-80]].
- **Ours has a cap:** {{c05.fails.guard-hit}} of these seeds reach it [[run:c05.fails.guard-hit]].

## What it combines with
@@combines

- **Erosion:** the talk also fires particles at a finished map, which its slide calls DLA for erosion [[t:191-193 s:21]]. See [erosion by aggregation](#dla-erode).

